0..77 Comment "// State as a theory: `get` passes the state to what runs after it, and `put`"
78..152 Comment "// replaces the state before what runs after it. The laws are the rules of"
153..226 Comment "// global state in Cooper, \"The marriage of effects and rewrites\" (2023),"
227..285 Comment "// § 2.1, oriented by the path order, one theory per law."
286..288 Comment "//"
289..356 Comment "// A put stores a value: no operation returns the sort `S`, so only"
357..434 Comment "// constructors and variables build a term of it. A continuation instantiated"
435..513 Comment "// at the stored value selects one branch of the abstraction a `get` holds and"
514..591 Comment "// calls no operation, so put-get descends as Cooper\'s branch selection does."
592..662 Comment "// Two of the laws in one theory overlap through a pattern, as get-get"
663..717 Comment "// overlaps itself; those are in the twin until #2116."
719..794 Comment "/// Storing a value and then reading the state is storing it and continuing"
795..805 Comment "/// at it."
